- categories: setter {Φ,Ψ,ε} / reducer {Σ,Κ,Υ,Β} / modulator (rest)
- uniform argument rule: setters consume literals; reducers return
  scalars; modulators act on context and pass values through
- dispatcher consults categories (replaces per-symbol special cases)
- Φπε proofs traceability TODOs: Φ boundedness (unclamped today),
  ε micro-ignition convergence (unbounded today), π spiral recursion
  (ceremonial today) — roadmap markers, not implementations
- 7 category tests: completeness, disjointness, per-category dispatch
